                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I'm not really a big fan of the Boomer Shooter genre of game (although I have a lot of FPS experience), but Amid Evil surprised me. The game isn't overly story-rich, but the world and level design itself is outstanding, and the pacing is perfect. There's many different episodes with a number of levels each, a good spread of weapons, and great variety in enemies. Each episode has a different theme that encompasses all of that episode's levels, and these themes are very well-executed. Level design/progression was a bit confusing one some levels, but that doesn't detract from this at all. There's par times for speed completions and attempting to speedrun the levels afterward I could see as genuine fun.\n\nEven on the game's hardest difficulty I originally found this game to be relatively easy, but I suppose that was just because I was actually trying to kill enemies gradually as they appeared. If you try to zoom through the levels, especially the later ones, it is a real challenge. That being said, the game has built-in cheats you can use with no penalty. You can even still get achievements. I'm guilty of this, because it was fun to essentially rocket-jump around the levels without any self-damage, although it trivializes the game depending on which ones you select. I do like that they don't take it too seriously in that regard.\n\nA few of said achievements were a bit buggy for me & required reloading to get them to trigger, and I fell through the map on two of the elevator platforms. Those were the only bugs I encountered. You can also die in Heaven.\n\nYou'll probably like this game if you don't mind a relative lack of engaging story, just fast-paced gameplay and well-crafted levels. The game is simply well-designed.",
